BusyBox 1.37.0 local modification for the A-SH Android terminal.

Changed by: Sylirre
Date of change: 2026-10-04 (modified-file notice added 2026-10-07)
License: GPL-2.0-only, as part of BusyBox (see BusyBox-LICENSE.txt)

The Android package manager only extracts native code named lib*.so, so the
BusyBox executable ships as libbusybox.so. This patch lets run_applet_and_exit()
treat that exact name like "busybox", and adds a prominent modified-file
notice (GPLv2 section 2(a)) to the changed file.

--- a/libbb/appletlib.c
+++ b/libbb/appletlib.c
@@ -10,6 +10,12 @@
  * Permission has been granted to redistribute this code under GPL.
  *
  * Licensed under GPLv2 or later, see file LICENSE in this source tree.
+ *
+ * MODIFIED FILE NOTICE (GPLv2 section 2(a)): changed by Sylirre on
+ * 2026-10-04 for the A-SH Android terminal (io.github.sylirre.terminal).
+ * run_applet_and_exit() also dispatches to busybox_main() when the binary
+ * is invoked under its APK packaging name "libbusybox.so".
+ * Not part of upstream BusyBox 1.37.0.
  */
 /* We are trying to not use printf, this benefits the case when selected
  * applets are really simple. Example:
@@ -977,7 +983,8 @@
 static NORETURN void run_applet_and_exit(const char *name, char **argv)
 {
 #  if ENABLE_BUSYBOX
-	if (is_prefixed_with(name, "busybox"))
+	/* A-SH Android (2026-10-04): accept the APK packaging name too. */
+	if (is_prefixed_with(name, "busybox") || strcmp(name, "libbusybox.so") == 0)
 		exit(busybox_main(/*unused:*/ 0, argv));
 #  endif
 #  if NUM_APPLETS > 0
